{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790299389,"nonce":"U45CYPzdd5o2IoMXSn+ACMjjVv4=","title":"Linux, --mode jit: a caught exception's stack loses the caller of a fully inlined throw","message":"test_trace_inlined in `--mode jit` on x86-64 Linux: exceptionStack after\n`try top(7)` lists leaf/mid/top but not `TestTraceInlined.main (line 28)`,\nwhich the interpreter prints. Found by the parity matrix's new jit row.\n\nThe frame-record chain that continues past the unwinder started at the\nlast compiled frame's CFA minus 16. The CFA the unwinder reports with a\ncompiled pc is its callee's (the slot at CFA-8 holds that pc), and on\nx86-64 Linux that callee is a runtime frame without a frame pointer, so the\nchain read garbage and stopped. Also, chained frames were ordered by the\nrecord address, which lies below the frame they return from, so the first\ncaller was discarded.","files":null}]}